# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in git and checked out LF on every platform.
# Without this, a Windows checkout produced CRLF working files while git held
# LF, so byte-size manifests (packages/components/file-sizes.json) measured
# differently in the main checkout, in a `git worktree`, and after a merge —
# and whole-file merge conflicts appeared where only two lines had changed.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is deliberate: it pins the working-tree
# ending too, so core.autocrlf on a contributor's machine cannot reintroduce
# the drift.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch the bytes.
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.docx  binary
